1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
This document defines the software requirements for the Competitive Programming Tracker.
The purpose of the system is to provide a centralized web application through which users can connect supported competitive-programming profiles, retrieve coding activity, monitor contest performance, analyze problem-solving progress, and track personal coding goals.
This document establishes the functional and non-functional requirements that will guide the product backlog, system architecture, database design, development, and testing activities.
---
2. Product Description
The Competitive Programming Tracker will be a full-stack web application designed primarily for students, competitive programmers, and coding-interview candidates.
The application will collect relevant information from supported competitive-programming platforms and present the information through a centralized dashboard.
The system will transform collected data into understandable statistics and visualizations that allow users to monitor their coding progress over time.
The initial implementation will focus on:
Web application development
User authentication
Profile management
External API integration
Data storage
Data processing
Performance analytics
Data visualization
Goal and progress tracking
---
3. Product Objectives
The primary objectives are:
OBJ-01 — Centralized Tracking
Provide users with a single platform for viewing relevant competitive-programming information.
OBJ-02 — Performance Monitoring
Allow users to monitor their coding activity and performance over time.
OBJ-03 — Statistical Analysis
Provide meaningful statistics based on contests, submissions, problems, ratings, topics, and difficulty levels.
OBJ-04 — Progress Visualization
Present coding progress using understandable charts, graphs, and other visual elements.
OBJ-05 — Goal Tracking
Allow users to define personal coding goals and monitor their progress.
OBJ-06 — Extensible Architecture
Build the application using a modular architecture that allows additional coding platforms and functionality to be introduced later.
---
4. Stakeholders
The primary stakeholders are:
4.1 End Users
Students, competitive programmers, and coding-interview candidates who use the platform to monitor their coding progress.
4.2 Project Administrator
The administrator responsible for managing users, platform content, and system-level operations.
4.3 Project Development Team
Developers responsible for designing, implementing, testing, deploying, and maintaining the application.
---
5. User Roles
The system will initially contain three user roles.
5.1 Guest
A visitor who has not authenticated.
Guest users can:
View the public landing page.
View general information about the application.
Register for an account.
Access the login page.
Guest users cannot access personalized coding data.
---
5.2 Registered User
An authenticated user.
Registered users can:
Manage their profile.
Connect supported coding-platform accounts.
Retrieve coding statistics.
View contest history.
View rating history.
View problem-solving statistics.
View performance analytics.
Create and manage personal goals.
Monitor progress.
---
5.3 Administrator
An authorized system administrator.
Administrators can:
Manage registered users.
View system information.
Manage application content where applicable.
Manage interview-preparation content if the module is enabled.
Monitor system-level operations.
---
6. Functional Requirements
Functional requirements define what the system must do.
---
6.1 User Registration
FR-001
The system shall allow a guest user to create an account.
FR-002
The registration process shall collect the minimum information required to create a user account.
FR-003
The system shall validate user-provided registration information.
FR-004
The system shall prevent creation of duplicate accounts according to the application's account-uniqueness rules.
FR-005
The system shall securely store user credentials.
---
7. User Authentication
FR-006
The system shall allow registered users to log in.
FR-007
The system shall validate authentication credentials before granting access to protected resources.
FR-008
The system shall allow authenticated users to log out.
FR-009
The system shall prevent unauthenticated users from accessing protected user information.
FR-010
The system shall provide appropriate authentication error messages.
---
8. User Profile Management
FR-011
The system shall provide each registered user with a profile.
FR-012
Users shall be able to view their profile information.
FR-013
