25. Out of Scope
The following are outside the initial implementation scope:
Building a competitive-programming platform from scratch
Hosting or executing user-submitted code
Replacing Codeforces or other coding platforms
Developing a mobile application
Direct modification of external coding-platform accounts
Collecting private information from external platforms without authorization
Advanced machine-learning functionality
Autonomous AI/agent systems
These may be reconsidered only through a formal change to the product scope.
---
26. Assumptions
The requirements are based on the following assumptions:
Users have accounts on supported competitive-programming platforms.
Required public data is accessible through supported APIs.
External APIs may change over time.
Users have internet access.
The initial application will primarily be accessed through a web browser.
Users are responsible for providing valid coding-platform usernames.
The project will initially prioritize a limited number of supported platforms.
---
27. Constraints
The project is subject to:
